#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md
#: 0323ed7f3c47404b8f7088f0f64004cd
msgid "Runtime"
msgstr "运行时"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md
#: 1df6a3835d984609afa9c785d1ea120f
msgid "Which compiled DSOs `switch_loadable_module_init()` loads"
msgstr "`switch_loadable_module_init()` 会加载哪些已编译的 DSO"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:30
#: 4022d0a298b24d3ca7bf77e95ba8746b
msgid ""
"`bootstrap.sh` copies `modules.conf.in` → `modules.conf` if missing. "
"Uncomment a `src/mod/...` line **after** bootstrap and **before** "
"`./configure` / `make`. A module can be compiled and still stay unloaded "
"if it is absent from the XML list."
msgstr ""
"若缺失，`bootstrap.sh` 会把 `modules.conf.in` 复制为 `modules.conf`。在 bootstrap "
"**之后**、`./configure` / `make` **之前** 取消注释某一行 `src/mod/...`。模块可以已编译，但若 XML"
" 列表里没有它，仍不会加载。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:32
#: e8db3d4197a94b6d8c4e3876f0e2fe61
msgid "How is `<load module=\"mod_sofia\"/>` parsed?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:34
#: 3aa82c91e5934b31be8a9b5aba7cc443
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"It is not a separate parser. Vanilla `freeswitch.xml` includes "
"`autoload_configs/*.xml` into the `configuration` section. After "
"`switch_xml_init()`, `switch_loadable_module_init()` calls "
"`switch_xml_open_cfg(\"modules.conf\")`, walks each `<load>` child, and "
"`dlopen`s `{mod_dir}/mod_sofia.so`. The exported table "
"`mod_sofia_module_interface` supplies `mod_sofia_load`. `reloadxml` does "
"not re-run that walk. Detail: "
"[Architecture](../1.architecture/01-architecture.md#runtime-load-tag), "
"[Workflows](../1.architecture/05-workflows.md#runtime-load-tag). What the"
" DSO registers after load: [Loadable module "
"contract](../1.architecture/01-architecture.md#loadable-module-contract)."
" Dispatch by name: [Interface registry "
"lookup](../1.architecture/05-workflows.md#interface-registry-lookup)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:36
#: 08f4885b83dd410b81f1fdee2d65ba1c
msgid "How do I load `mod_xml_rpc` and serve a portal page?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:38
#: b89238cb2b834cd39db0933d86cf22c5
msgid ""
"`mod_xml_rpc` must be enabled in the build-time `modules.conf` as "
"`xml_int/mod_xml_rpc` and in the runtime "
"`autoload_configs/modules.conf.xml` with `<load "
"module=\"mod_xml_rpc\"/>`. Its settings are in "
"`autoload_configs/xml_rpc.conf.xml`; the default HTTP port is **8080**. "
"The module exposes XML-RPC at `/RPC2`, API wrappers at `/api/`, "
"`/webapi/`, `/txtapi/`, and `/xmlapi/`, and serves static files from "
"`htdocs_dir`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:47
#: 1affad1cabd24c2d9f197069c38ce097
msgid ""
"It is an HTTP server and static-file mechanism, not a complete "
"administration UI. Put a portal entry page at "
"`<htdocs_dir>/portal/index.html`; requesting `/portal` redirects there. "
"The bundled starter assets are under `htdocs/portal/`. Set all three "
"`auth-realm`, `auth-user`, and `auth-pass` parameters to protect "
"non-`/pub` requests with Basic Authentication. The sample credentials are"
" for demonstration only; use a strong password and restrict port 8080 "
"with a firewall, VPN, or HTTPS reverse proxy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:55
#: dca167c433cc4b5980c1e8a61582efca
msgid "Why is there no IDL for modules?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:57
#: 9879b022637549fe8924328a15bec6fe
msgid ""
"Modules and core share `switch.h` in one process. Load registers **name +"
" function pointer** into hashes (`application_hash`, `api_hash`, "
"`endpoint_hash`, …). Dialplan `application=\"bridge\"` and `api status` "
"are lookups, not RPC stubs. [Loadable module "
"contract](../1.architecture/01-architecture.md#loadable-module-contract)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:59
#: 550c1c68ed824eb29076d95878f36bc6
msgid "What is the default prefix, and how do I start FreeSWITCH?"
msgstr "默认 prefix 是什么，怎样启动 FreeSWITCH？"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:61
#: 4a1e6d207ce849e29e3ba71ff0c64bea
msgid ""
"Default prefix without `--prefix` is `/usr/local/freeswitch` "
"(`configure.ac`). The PKB developer path uses `--prefix=\"$HOME/fs\" "
"--disable-fhs` so the installed files stay below that prefix. A custom "
"prefix without `--disable-fhs` uses FHS paths."
msgstr ""
"不带 `--prefix` 时默认前缀为 `/usr/local/freeswitch`（`configure.ac`）。PKB 开发者路径使用 "
"`--prefix=\"$HOME/fs\" --disable-fhs`，因此安装文件都位于该前缀下。未指定 `--disable-fhs` "
"的自定义前缀使用 FHS 路径。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:70
#: bae3f92705ab402493f0d74711a6503c
msgid ""
"`-ncwait`: background, no console, wait until the core is ready "
"(`src/switch.c`). `-nonat`: skip UPnP/NAT-PMP pinholes — required unless "
"you *want* auto-NAT (`conf/vanilla/README_IMPORTANT.txt`). Foreground: "
"`freeswitch -c -nonat`. Stop: `freeswitch -stop`. Debian systemd uses "
"`/usr/bin/freeswitch -u freeswitch -g freeswitch -ncwait -nonat`."
msgstr ""
"`-ncwait`：后台、无控制台，等到核心就绪（`src/switch.c`）。`-nonat`：跳过 UPnP/NAT-PMP 打洞 — "
"除非你 *想要* 自动 NAT，否则必须加（`conf/vanilla/README_IMPORTANT.txt`）。前台：`freeswitch"
" -c -nonat`。停止：`freeswitch -stop`。Debian systemd 使用 `/usr/bin/freeswitch "
"-u freeswitch -g freeswitch -ncwait -nonat`。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:72
#: b3ce723edfd441cdad69be334cfc69be
msgid "How do I prove FreeSWITCH is up?"
msgstr "怎样证明 FreeSWITCH 已经起来？"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:78
#: 74499d905d17404392e73dd77eade846
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Working output starts with `UP` (same check as "
"`docker/base_image/healthcheck.sh`, regex `^UP`). Then `fs_cli -x sofia "
"status` for SIP profiles. If `fs_cli` cannot connect, the switch may be "
"down, `mod_event_socket` may not be loaded, the client target may not "
"reach the listener, **or the source IP failed the Event Socket ACL**. "
"`fs_cli` defaults to `127.0.0.1:8021`; vanilla listens on `::`:8021. "
"Loopback works while the host LAN IP is rejected until you set `apply-"
"inbound-acl` — [Remote Event Socket ACL](../5.operations/01-runbook.md"
"#remote-event-socket-acl)."
msgstr ""
"正常输出会以 `UP` 开头（与 `docker/base_image/healthcheck.sh` 相同，正则为 `^UP`）。然后运行 "
"`fs_cli -x sofia status` 检查 SIP 配置档。如果 `fs_cli` "
"无法连接，交换机可能未运行、`mod_event_socket` 可能未加载，或客户端目标无法访问服务端监听器。`fs_cli` 默认连接 "
"`127.0.0.1:8021`；vanilla 监听 `::`:8021，因此请检查主机的 IPv4/IPv6 套接字行为。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:80
#: 99f99bba9b1641468ee55040fa71e9e4
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First call without a second phone: register as `1000` / password `1234` "
"on port 5060, then dial **`9196`** (echo). See [Quick Start](../0"
".getting-started/02-quick-start.md) and [Users Manual Chapter "
"2](https://developer.signalwire.com/freeswitch/foundations/getting-"
"started)."
msgstr ""
"没有第二部话机时的首呼：以 `1000` / 密码 `1234` 在 5060 端口注册，然后拨 **`9196`**（回声）。见 "
"[快速开始](01-quick-start.md) 与 [用户手册第 2 "
"章](https://developer.signalwire.com/freeswitch/foundations/getting-"
"started)。"

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:82
#: 32f080912cb04045875f6fa7960c7745
msgid "How do I track a SIP call from the log?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:84
#: 3f2ae77206b64da393b0e47f80556b8b
msgid ""
"Correlate with the **channel UUID**, not the SIP `Call-ID`. Core logs "
"attach the UUID via `SWITCH_CHANNEL_SESSION_LOG` (`mod_logfile` prefixes "
"it when `uuid=true`). Channel events use header **`Unique-ID`**. A-leg "
"and B-leg each have their own UUID; `show channels` lists `uuid` per leg "
"and **`call_uuid`** to join them (`show calls` uses `b_uuid` on the "
"paired view). SIP `Call-ID` is a signaling identifier — it appears in "
"siptrace, not as the file-logger prefix. Step-by-step grep / `/uuid` / "
"`bridge_uuid` / CDR: [Runbook — Follow one call by channel "
"UUID](../5.operations/01-runbook.md#follow-one-call-by-channel-uuid). "
"Column meanings and a captured two-leg `bridge`: [Workflows — show "
"channels during a bridge](../1.architecture/05-workflows.md#worked-"
"example-show-channels-during-a-bridge)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:86
#: cb61d6a012334f47bf48079a31e22bd9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Vanilla console is **`info`** (`$${console_loglevel}`). For one inbound "
"call:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:88
#: ee94f68285dd4299959911c9115eb856
msgid ""
"Note the time, then `fs_cli -x 'show channels'` while the call is up (or "
"`show calls` after). Copy the UUID (truncate in notes if you will share "
"the log). A custom dialplan `log` line (for example `hit test_1005 "
"uuid=…`) is another way to recover the UUID after hangup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:89
#: f13388e6865e447283e4c4d52cb5dd46
msgid ""
"Follow `$log_dir/freeswitch.log` (`$prefix/log/freeswitch.log` on a "
"prefix install). On the source Docker image (`-nf`): `docker logs -f "
"--since=10s freeswitch`, or `docker exec … tail -F "
"/usr/local/freeswitch/log/freeswitch.log`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:90
#: b5e6054884194c7f8c5eccf073d928ee
msgid ""
"`sofia profile internal siptrace on` dumps **tport** bytes (Sofia-SIP), "
"before `sofia_event_callback`. Packet-to-session hop: "
"[Workflows](../1.architecture/05-workflows.md#packet-path-udptcp-to-nua)."
" Those lines often omit the channel UUID — also grep `uuid_getvar <uuid> "
"sip_call_id`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:91
#: d8036b69eea942e7977a35fb233f8580
msgid ""
"Filter: `fs_cli` `/uuid <channel-uuid>` (clear with `/uuid`), or grep the"
" file logger for that UUID. Typical order: Sofia `recv` INVITE → "
"`Processing … in context …` → `EXECUTE` apps → `Hangup … [CS_EXECUTE] "
"[<cause>]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:93
#: 3afef9b4e28e413d800d6b3dcd1a837a
msgid ""
"A **407** then a second **INVITE** is Digest (`Proxy-Authenticate`); a "
"**401** then a second **REGISTER** is the same math with `WWW-"
"Authenticate`. Neither challenge is by itself a failure. `EXECUTE … "
"ivr(demo_ivr)` plus `mod_sndfile` “No such file or directory” under "
"`sounds/en/us/callie/ivr/` means missing Callie prompts (`make sounds-"
"install`), not a SIP routing miss. Redact `Proxy-Authorization`, nonces, "
"full UUIDs, and `Call-ID` before sharing. Full command list: "
"[Observability](../5.operations/02-observability.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:95
#: 195941bed3eb465f85f67abb69d62c03
msgid "How do I read `show channels`?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Users/walterfan/workspace/walter/freeswitch_primer/man/7.appendix/02-faq.md:97
#: f82953a3bb9b4902955d7534bfe31b26
msgid ""
"`fs_cli -x 'show channels'` dumps the core SQL `channels` scoreboard as "
